<title>HONG KONG: SHK &amp; Co slides on rights issue plan.</title>
<headline>SHK &amp; Co slides on rights issue plan.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Sun Hung Kai &amp; Co fell sharply in early Thursday trade after the company announced a rights issue to raise a total HK$498 million.</p>
<p>The stock was down HK$0.325 at HK$2.075 on volume of 1.7 million shares.</p>
<p>&quot;The rights issue is unwelcome by the market since most of the money will be used for loan repayment,&quot; said Ben Kwong, research director at Dharmala Securities.</p>
<p>Trading of Sun Hung Kai shares resumed on Thursday after being suspended on Wednesday pending the announcement of the two-for-five rights issue plan at HK$1.80 per rights share.</p>
<p>-- HONG KONG NEWSROOM (852) 2843 6369</p>
